<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH SUNDAY LEAGUE RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH SUNDAY LEAGUE RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of rain-affected English</p>
<p>Sunday league (40 overs) cricket matches:</p>
<p>At Darlington: Kent beat Durham by 16 runs. Kent 141 in 39.5</p>
<p>overs (A.Walker 4-18, J.Wood 4-17). Durham 125 in 34.2 overs.</p>
<p>Kent 4 points.</p>
<p>At Bristol: Gloucestershire beat Middlesex by 55 runs.</p>
<p>Gloucestershire 232-6 innings closed (S.Young 89 not out,</p>
<p>M.Lynch 53). Middlesex 177-6 in 38 overs (O.Shah 65 not out).</p>
<p>Gloucestershire 4 points.</p>
<p>At Northampton: Northamptonshire beat Hampshire by four</p>
<p>wickets. Hampshire 159-2 in 23 overs (M.Hayden 54, J.Laney 53).</p>
<p>Northamptonshire 174-6 in 22.4 overs (R.Bailey 50). Northants 4</p>
<p>points.</p>
<p>At Trent Bridge: Nottinghamshire beat Yorkshire by 13 runs.</p>
<p>Nottinghamshire 169-4 in 30 overs, innings closed (A.Metcalfe 70</p>
<p>not out). Yorkshire 78-5 in 15 overs. Notts 4 points.</p>
<p>At Bath: Leicestershire beat Somerset by 17 runs.</p>
<p>Leicestershire 166-8 in 31 overs, innings closed. Somerset 30-1</p>
<p>in 11 overs. Leicestershire 4 points.</p>
<p>At Worcester: Worcestershire beat Surrey by seven wickets.</p>
<p>Surrey 149 in 37 overs (M.Bicknell 57 not out; G.Haynes 4-13).</p>
<p>Worcestershire 150-3 in 31.3 overs.</p>
<p>At Old Trafford: Lancashire v Glamorgan - match abandoned. 2</p>
<p>points each.</p>
<p>At Derby: Derbyshire v Sussex - match abandoned. 2 points</p>
<p>each.</p>
</text>
